INT. ORBITAL LAUNDROMAT - ZERO-G - NIGHT CYCLE

A ring-shaped station module lined with front-loading machines. Wet clothes drift in loose clouds. Each dryer window glows green. A hand-stamped sign reads: "NO SOCKS IN THE VENT."

DOROTHY OKONKWO-REYES (40s, mag-boots, plaid shirt tucked in) sits strapped to a bench. LUDWIG ABDELKADER (60s, quilted vest) floats upside down above the folding table. KALINDA ROSENBAUM-PRICE (20s, a cloud of dark hair held down by a net) clings to a handhold by the change machine. And a big, quiet man, THADDEUS MWANGI-COLE (50s, a toolbelt, a single sock stuck to his forehead), hovers by the airlock.

DOROTHY
Who put the red one in with the whites?

LUDWIG
It wasn't me.

KALINDA
It wasn't me.

DOROTHY
Then who?

LUDWIG
Dorothy, we are four people on a ring in orbit. It was one of us.

KALINDA
Or the ring.

DOROTHY
The ring doesn't do laundry.

LUDWIG
It does everything else.

THADDEUS
(peeling the sock from his forehead)
It was me.

All three turn. Thaddeus holds up the red shirt. Pink cloth drifts around it like a nebula.

DOROTHY
Thaddeus.

THADDEUS
I thought it would blend.

KALINDA
It blended.

LUDWIG
Everything is now the color of a salmon.

DOROTHY
Our uniforms were white!

THADDEUS
They're coral now.

KALINDA
(whisper)
It's not a bad look.

LUDWIG
Kalinda!

KALINDA
What? It isn't.

Dorothy unclips from the bench, kicks off, and sails across the module to the nearest dryer. She slaps it. The drum slows. Pink socks and shirts tumble in the green glow.

DOROTHY
(softly)
Nobody mention this at the briefing.

LUDWIG
Agreed.

KALINDA
Agreed.

THADDEUS
Agreed.

The dryer chimes. A single white sock floats free.
